# `DfoBuilder::with_problem`

[Back to `dfo::DfoBuilder`](../DfoBuilder.md)

Replaces the whole problem.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::DfoBuilder dfo::DfoBuilder::with_problem(const dfo::DfoProblem &problem) const;
```

## What It Does

Swaps in a complete [`DfoProblem`](../DfoProblem.md), keeping the options already collected. Use it to start from a problem value built elsewhere and still add settings with the chained calls.

## Parameters

`const dfo::DfoProblem &problem`
: The problem to use.

## Returns

A new builder with the change; the original is untouched.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A problem value, then a setting.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::DfoProblem problem;
  problem.initial = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  problem.objective = f;
  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build().with_problem(problem).with_solver(dfo::DfoSolverKind::PatternSearch).solve();
  out.writeln(dfo::to_string(r.selected_solver), ", minimizer =", r.minimizer.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2

Options survive the swap. The seed set before `with_problem` still applies.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::DfoProblem problem;
  problem.initial = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  problem.objective = f;
  const dfo::DfoBuilder tuned = dfo::DFO::build().with_seed(7).with_max_evaluations(200);
  out.writeln("seed =", tuned.with_problem(problem).options().rng_seed, ", budget =", tuned.with_problem(problem).options().max_evaluations);
}
```

### Example 3

Replacing a problem. The second `with_problem` discards the first problem's objective.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::DfoProblem a, b;
  a.initial = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  a.objective = f;
  b.initial = pluss::series::make({1.0});
  b.objective = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 5.0).square().sum(); };
  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build().with_problem(a).with_problem(b).solve();
  out.writeln("minimizer =", r.minimizer.items<double>());
}
```

